    "result_text": "Build succeeds. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the daily-limit rule for `POST /api/owners`: the 100th owner registered today is fine, the 101st is rejected with **429 Too Many Requests**.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor idiom (mirroring the existing `EnsureCityCapacity` rule), I added small, self-contained units rather than growing any existing method:\n\n- **`EnsureDailyLimit`** (new function) \u2014 counts owners whose `registrationDate` equals today; throws `DailyLimitExceededException` at \u2265100.\n- **`DailyLimitExceededException`** (new checked exception).\n- **`DailyLimitExceededExceptionHandler`** (new handler) \u2014 responds 429.\n- **Escalation YAML** mapping the exception to its handler.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 one inserted step (`ensureDailyLimit`) wired between `ensureCityCapacity` and `build`.\n\nStructural impact is kept low: the only edited existing function is none \u2014 the sole existing-file edit is a two-line rewire of the YAML pipeline. Every new class has one public method with no surrounding-class complexity to hold. All tests green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
